 ## Overview
-Multi-Level Hashed Grid Construction is a method for rapidly building an acceleration structure that combines the render-time performance of multi-level grids with the low memory footprint of hashed grids [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high memory consumption in classic multi-level array grids and the poor traversal performance of one-level hashed grids for large, sparse scanned scenes [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Hash Grids](936-hash-grids.md) by adding macrocells to skip empty regions during traversal, and from [Voxel World Data Structure](1101-voxel-world-data-structure.md) by using row displacement compression to eliminate empty cells entirely [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Multi-Level Hashed Grid Construction is a method for rapidly building an acceleration structure that combines the render-time performance of multi-level grids with the low memory footprint of hashed grids [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high memory consumption in classic multi-level array grids and the poor traversal performance of one-level hashed grids for large, sparse scanned scenes [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Hash Grids](936-hash-grids.md) by adding macrocells to skip empty regions during traversal, and from [Voxel World Data Structure](1101-voxel-world-data-structure.md) by using row displacement compression to eliminate empty cells entirely [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
